# NOT the active .dockerignore for `docker-compose build` or `docker build`
# run from inside frontend/ or backend/ — Docker only reads .dockerignore
# from the build context directory, so see frontend/.dockerignore and
# backend/.dockerignore for those. This root file only matters if you build
# with the repo root as context (e.g. `docker build -f backend/Dockerfile .`).
# Without an ignore file in the actual context dir, `COPY . .` would pick up
# whatever happens to be sitting locally in that folder — most importantly:
#   - node_modules: COPY runs *after* the image's own `npm ci`, so a local
#     node_modules present when running `docker build` on your own machine
#     would silently overwrite the freshly-installed one with host-platform
#     native bindings (e.g. bcrypt compiled for macOS won't run in the
#     Alpine/Linux container) — a "works locally, crashes in Docker" bug.
#   - .env: would get baked directly into an image layer, leaking secrets.
# Railway builds from git (which already excludes these via .gitignore), so
# this mainly protects local `docker build` / `docker compose build` testing
# before you push — but costs nothing to have either way.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.log
**/uploads/*
!**/uploads/.gitkeep
.git
.github
*.zip
**/.DS_Store
